      "content": "thanks for that. it's a good start but honestly i'm a bit worried about the flow. it feels a little \"heavy\" in some places.\n\ni just checked something—i ran a rough check on how these things usually get flagged, and it seems like if the density of those specific terms is too low, the automated filter might just toss the application before a human even sees it. \n\ncan we do another version? i need you to make sure the \"high-impact\" terms are more prominent so i don't get filtered out, but please, i'm serious, try to keep it from sounding like a thesaurus exploded. it still needs to sound like a real academic wrote it, not an algorithm. can you try to integrate them more robustly?",
